            <field>
              <name>SRAM0PMS</name>
              <description>System SRAM0 In Bank0 Power Mode Select (Write Protect)\nThis field can control SRAM0 in bank0 (64k) power mode for range 0x2010_0000 - 0x2010_FFFF.\nNote 1: Power shut down mode can get least leakage, but don't guarantee the retention of SRAM data.\nNote 2: This bit is write protected. Refer to the SYS_REGLCTL register.\nNote 3: Write operation is ignored when PCBUSY is 1.\nNote 4: These bits are not retained when D3 power is turned off.</description>
