            </field>
            <field>
              <name>CLKERRIF</name>
              <description>Clock Error Interrupt Status\nWhen the frequency of 32.768 kHz external low speed crystal oscillator (LXT) or 12 MHz internal high speed RC oscillator (HIRC) is shift larger to unreasonable value, this bit will be set and to be an indicate that clock frequency is inaccuracy\nOnce this bit is set to 1, the auto trim operation stopped and FREQSEL(SYS_TCTL12M[1:0]) will be cleared to 00 by hardware automatically if CESTOPEN(SYS_TCTL12M[8]) is set to 1.\nIf this bit is set and CLKEIEN(SYS_IRCTIEN[2]) is high, an interrupt will be triggered to notify the clock frequency is inaccuracy.\nNote: Write 1 to clear this bit to 0.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <enumeratedValues>
                 <enumeratedValue>
